  "body": "Originally designed by architectural designer Trevor Pyle, the home was created around a philosophy of natural materials, passive-solar design and healthy-home principles - ideas that were remarkably forward-thinking when the house was built and remain just as relevant today. \r\n\r\nFrom its storybook cedar exterior and distinctive gables to its warm natural timber interiors, 5A Marie Avenue feels like a little piece of Europe tucked away on the Red Beach coast.\r\n\r\nThe clever thinking is beautifully woven into the home. Large wooden beams and sarked ceilings bring warmth and character throughout, while double glazed windows some fitted with fly screens and carefully considered orientation capture and retain the movement of the sun from morning through to afternoon and evening. Even the fireplace was designed with earth-brick thermal mass, absorbing heat from the fire and releasing it back into the home over time.\r\n\r\nBut ultimately, what makes this house so special is how effortlessly it all comes together. Warm, welcoming and wonderfully different, it has an almost French-country feel that transports you somewhere far from suburban Auckland.\r\n\r\nThe heart of the home is the open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, where every space flows naturally to the outdoors. Expansive kwila decking wraps around the home, creating beautiful places to dine, relax and entertain, while the covered pergola and spa pool are made for long summer evenings and catching the afternoon and evening sun.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the private master retreat feels like a world of its own, complete with bathroom and one of the home's most charming surprises - an internal shuttered window that opens to overlook the living room below. It's a wonderfully unexpected detail that connects the levels and adds to the sense of discovery.\r\n\r\nThen there's the space above the garage - a world of its own. Completely separate from the main house, it includes a large study and bathroom, making it ideal for teenagers, guests, extended family, a creative studio or working from home. Add generous off-street parking for three cars and you've got flexibility that's increasingly hard to find.\r\n\r\nAnd then there's the beach. It's so close you can hear it. Enjoy morning walks, afternoon swims and a short stroll to the local Surf Club. This is coastal living at its best in a house that isn't just a house. It's a home meticulously crafted, with character and a lifestyle you'll fall in love with.\r\n\r\nCall Paul or Jayde today to find out more or see you at one of the open homes.",
